# Sensitive files (auto-detected)
.env
build
# build_and_install.bat / build_and_install.sh were listed here by the
# auto-detector, but they hold no secrets: they READ .env and pass only
# SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY to --dart-define. Ignoring them meant the
# only script that knows how to build a release APK which actually reaches the
# backend lived on a single laptop -- a fresh clone had no script, ran a bare
# `flutter build apk`, and silently shipped an offline-only app.
flutter_01.log
# "Masjid-app.apk (large file: 65MB)" was here, which is not a valid pattern --
# the parenthetical made it match nothing. Ignore the real filename instead.
Masjid-app.apk
